From b0034b1fd56542602f34752c4d17249819cbe9f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Braga?= <code@andrebraga.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:59:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(Source Device): wait for input instead of polling when
 idle

Every evdev source slept up to 2.5 ms between non-blocking reads, and
every target device ticked every 4-8 ms to look for output events, so
an idle handheld woke InputPlumber over a thousand times a second.

Sources with a pollable fd now wait for it to become readable: input
wakes the loop at once, and after a second without events the wait
stretches to 100 ms so queued output commands are still serviced.
Target devices keep their poll rate while active and fall back to
100 ms after a second without commands, output or scheduled events.
